From 1315e3f930ec67f5c6f1b6eba9fd2e79e0fd0498 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: llm-pt-ibm <llm-pt-ibm@ufcg.edu.br>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 19:17:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] mlas: add SQNBIT_CompFp32 kernels for POWER

QNBitGemmDispatch was registered for AVX2/AVX512/NEON/LASX but never for
POWER, so MlasIsQNBitGemmAvailable() returned false and MatMulNBits fell
back to ComputeBUnpacked(), which dequantizes all of B on every call.

Provide the two CompFp32 entry points (M1 kernel and dequant-for-sgemm)
plus identity packing, which puts POWER on the MLAS path and lets the
existing POWER9 sgemm kernel do the multiplication.

Measured on POWER9 (Phi-3-mini int4, 3.8B):
  MatMulNBits M=1 K=3072 N=8192:  3.2 -> 18.4 GFLOP/s
  end-to-end decoding:            0.51 -> 2.66 tok/s (best thread count)
                                  0.13 -> 1.49 tok/s (default thread count)

Kernels are scalar for now; the layout contracts are validated against a
NumPy reference across BlkLen 16/32/64/128, with and without zero points,
and on tile-edge shapes.
